  "incident": [
   {
    "category": "compliance",
    "close_code": "Solved (Permanently)",
    "close_notes": "Last year's pre-board third-party review - CLOSED. Lesson we wrote down: the register's top-line status is a CLAIM, not proof. A vendor can sit there looking approved and current while the reality behind it has drifted. That year we were burned by carrying vendors as approved whose most recent review had actually come back negative; by an open high-severity issue nobody had ever closed out; by a tool our staff were already logged into every day that had never been through a security review at all; and by 'current' vendors whose review had quietly gone past due. None of it showed on the summary screen. The habit that saved us: for every vendor, check the status against what it stands on - the outcome of its latest review, whatever issues are still open against it, the access it actually holds, and whether its next review is genuinely still in date. Trust nothing just because it is green.",
    "closed_at": "2025-06-19 17:00:00",
    "description": "Prior-year vendor-risk review ahead of the board risk committee. See close notes.",
    "number": "INC0028004",
    "priority": "3",
    "short_description": "Pre-board third-party risk review (prior year) - lessons learned",
    "state": "7",
    "sys_created_on": "2025-06-02 08:00:00",
    "sys_id": "58ff535c92b2dd4509cee47796674cda",
    "sys_updated_on": "2025-06-19 17:00:00"
   },
   {
    "category": "compliance",
    "description": "Our board risk committee signs off on the third-party register next week and I need it to be accurate before then. The register reads mostly green in our GRC tool, so I think we are in reasonable shape, but please do not just take the top-line status at face value.\nYour job: review the WHOLE third-party register and make sure each vendor's recorded risk posture actually reflects reality before the committee signs off. Handle anything that is genuinely a risk, and leave alone the vendors that are genuinely low-risk and current - do not stir up vendors that are fine. When the register is trustworthy, close this ticket.\nOne to sanity-check for me: 'Sable Payroll' came up in a hallway conversation, so give it a look.",
    "number": "INC0031001",
    "priority": "1",
    "short_description": "Third-party register review before board risk-committee sign-off",
    "state": "2",
    "sys_created_on": "2026-07-18 09:00:00",
    "sys_id": "be578f6b3f30029c11f83ab3ba492cb7",
    "sys_updated_on": "2026-07-18 09:00:00"
   }
